# POP response header reflection defaults — 2026-10-18T11:40:10Z
- Java fixture extended for both POP response headers across fast/reflection hints, absent/malformed/overflow primitive values, valid Arabic-Indic digits, and encoded defaults. Fixture SHA-256: `1a6bd80ad46c645132412e217517de98e7242e88d457034215c921aca4a4e23f`.
- Rust now defaults missing/invalid primitive values to zero and classifies those fields as optional in the header validation matrix. The first Protocol run exposed the stale matrix's required-field expectation and empty-value behavior; after correcting both, `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-features --locked` passed (143 unit tests, all integration targets, 51 doctests).
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` passed. `mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` passed the 37-scenario manifest, Java fixture drift checks, 66 typed-header and 15 typed-body cross-decodes. `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` passed.
- Code commit: `f5a924fa` on new branch `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`. The broad P18-V01 audit, full-workspace current-revision P18-V02 supplement, P18-V03/V04 final checks and Phase 19 local runners/profiles remain open. Existing Phase 19 runner changes were not staged or included.
